# Outbound calling + human agent takeover (LiveKit path).
#
# Requires LIVEKIT_MODE=selfhost, a running agent worker (`npm run agent`), and a public
# HOST tunnel — Twilio fetches the answer webhook and the status callbacks over it.
#
# Flow: this endpoint dials, Twilio rings the contact, and ONLY on answer does Twilio fetch
# /outbound-answer for the bridge TwiML. That is why the agent never greets a ringing phone.

@base_url = http://localhost:5070/api/phone-call/twilio
@contact = +6281928200568
# +6281928200568

### Place an outbound call — uses the ServeAI prompt/greeting as-is
POST {{base_url}}/outbound-call
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "to": "{{contact}}"
}

### Place an outbound call with a per-call instruction and greeting
# `instruction` replaces the ServeAI prompt for this call only; `greeting` is the first
# line the agent speaks once the contact picks up. chatflowId and the liveKitSTT/liveKitTTS
# legs still come from ServeAI config, so the agent keeps its knowledge-base and
# appointment tools on outbound calls.
#
# Response: { "success": true, "callSid": "CAxxxx", "token": "...", "to": "+62..." }
# Keep the callSid — the transfer endpoint below needs it.
POST {{base_url}}/outbound-call
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "to": "{{contact}}",
  "greeting": "Hello, I'm calling from Restaurant Entier. Am I speaking with Friendly?"
}

### Trigger a human takeover manually (normally the agent's transferToHumanAgent tool does this)
# Dials HUMAN_AGENT_NUMBER (or ServeAI's humanAgentPhoneNumber) into a waiting conference,
# then redirects the caller in. That redirect ends the LiveKit bridge — a COLD handoff, so
# the agent leaves. Both legs are then forked to the transcriber and their turns land in
# the same ServeAI chatroom as the AI half of the call.
#
# callerNumber is REQUIRED: it seeds the ServeAI chatroom lookup. Omit it and the human
# conversation is written to a brand-new chatroom instead of the caller's.
POST {{base_url}}/transfer-to-human
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "callSid": "CAxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx",
  "chatflowId": "your-chatflow-id",
  "callerNumber": "6285725868168"
}
